MetaWINDOW supports the following operating systems
and runtime environments:

     MetaWINDOW-DOS
       MSDOS or PCDOS (real-mode ) V3.0 to present.

     MetaWINDOW-DOS/286
       Borland 286 DOS-Extender (Turbo Pascal 7.0)
       Phar Lap 286 DOS-Extender
       Rational Systems DOS/16M 286 DOS-Extender

     MetaWINDOW-DOS/386
       Phar Lap 386 DOS-Extender
       Rational Systems DOS/4G 386 DOS-Extender
       Watcom 4GW 386 DOS-Extender

  Note that MetaWINDOW/286 and 386 use full
  protected mode code.  No CPU time is wasted 
  switching back and forth to real mode 
  to draw!!
  
  MetaWINDOW/286 for 16 bit DOS extenders 
  is fully DPMI 0.9 compliant and has been 
  tested under MS-Windows.

  MetaWINDOW/386 for 32 bit DOS extenders 
  is true 32 code, assembled from a 
  separate source than the 16-bit libraries.

  MetaWINDOW's speed makes it ideal for real-
  time applications.  While not directly supported
  by Metagraphics, many customers are successfully
  using MetaWINDOW with real-time protected-mode
  kernals such as 'VRTX' from Ready Systems and
  'Nucleus' from Accelerated Technology.
   

